To implement the search functionality and display a comparison of photos based on price, name, and description, we need to extend both the backend and frontend functionalities. Below is a detailed plan and corresponding code snippets to achieve this:

### Backend Implementation

First, we will enhance the backend to support searching through photos. The `/search` endpoint will allow users to search through photos based on the `name` or `description`.

```python
@app.route('/search', methods=['GET'])
def search_photos():
    query = request.args.get('query', '')
    conn = sqlite3.connect('photos.db')
    c = conn.cursor()
    c.execute("SELECT * FROM photos WHERE name LIKE ? OR description LIKE ?", ('%' + query + '%', '%' + query + '%'))
    results = c.fetchall()
    conn.close()

    # Format results for JSON response
    formatted_results = [{"name": r[1], "price": r[2], "description": r[3], "filename": r[4]} for r in results]
    return jsonify(formatted_results)
```

#### Sorting Endpoint

The `/compare` endpoint will allow sorting photos by `price`, `name`, or `description`.

```python
@app.route('/compare', methods=['GET'])
def compare_photos():
    sort_by = request.args.get('sort_by', 'price')  # Default sorting by price
    order = request.args.get('order', 'asc')  # Default ascending order
    conn = sqlite3.connect('photos.db')
    c = conn.cursor()
    c.execute(f"SELECT * FROM photos ORDER BY {sort_by} {order.upper()}")
    results = c.fetchall()
    conn.close()

    # Format results for JSON response
    formatted_results = [{"name": r[1], "price": r[2], "description": r[3], "filename": r[4]} for r in results]
    return jsonify(formatted_results)
```

### Frontend Implementation

Next, we will modify the frontend to include a search bar and a dropdown menu to sort photos.

#### MainActivity.java

In `MainActivity.java`, we will add a search bar and a dropdown menu to sort photos.

```java
public class MainActivity extends AppCompatActivity {

    private ApiService apiService;
    private List<Photo> photos;

    @Override
    protected void onCreate(Bundle savedInstanceState) {
        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState);
        setContentView(R.layout.activity_main);

        // Initialize Retrofit
        Retrofit retrofit = new Retrofit.Builder()
                .baseUrl("http://your_backend_url/")
                .addConverterFactory(GsonConverterFactory.create())
                .build();

        apiService = retrofit.create(ApiService.class);

        // Set up spinner for sorting options
        Spinner spinnerSortBy = findViewById(R.id.spinnerSortBy);
        ArrayAdapter<CharSequence> adapter = ArrayAdapter.createFromResource(this,
                R.array.sort_by_options, android.R.layout.simple_spinner_item);
        adapter.setDropDownViewResource(android.R.layout.simple_spinner_dropdown_item);
        spinnerSortBy.setAdapter(adapter);

        // Fetch and display photos
        fetchPhotos("price", "asc");

        // Handle spinner selection
        spinnerSortBy.setOnItemSelectedListener(new AdapterView.OnItemSelectedListener() {
            @Override
            public void onItemSelected(AdapterView<?> parent, View view, int position, long id) {
                String sortBy = parent.getItemAtPosition(position).toString();
                fetchPhotos(sortBy, "asc");
            }

            @Override
            public void onNothingSelected(AdapterView<?> parent) {}
        });

        // Set up search functionality
        EditText editTextSearch = findViewById(R.id.editTextSearch);
        editTextSearch.addTextChangedListener(new TextWatcher() {
            @Override
            public void beforeTextChanged(CharSequence s, int start, int count, int after) {}

            @Override
            public void onTextChanged(CharSequence s, int start, int before, int count) {
                searchPhotos(s.toString());
            }

            @Override
            public void afterTextChanged(Editable s) {}
        });
    }

    private void fetchPhotos(String sortBy, String order) {
        Call<List<Photo>> call = apiService.getSortedPhotos(sortBy, order);
        call.enqueue(new Callback<List<Photo>>() {
            @Override
            public void onResponse(Call<List<Photo>> call, Response<List<Photo>> response) {
                if (response.isSuccessful()) {
                    photos = response.body();
                    // Update UI with photos
                }
            }

            @Override
            public void onFailure(Call<List<Photo>> call, Throwable t) {
                // Handle failure
            }
        });
    }

    private void searchPhotos(String query) {
        Call<List<Photo>> call = apiService.searchPhotos(query);
        call.enqueue(new Callback<List<Photo>>() {
            @Override
            public void onResponse(Call<List<Photo>> call, Response<List<Photo>> response) {
                if (response.isSuccessful()) {
                    List<Photo> photos = response.body();
                    // Update UI with photos
                }
            }

            @Override
            public void onFailure(Call<List<Photo>> call, Throwable t) {
                // Handle failure
            }
        });
    }
}
```

This implementation ensures that users can easily search through photos and view them sorted by various attributes, enhancing the usability and functionality of the app.
